{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DvaxqTFair7rDbQGmkykGW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted results for each planned experiment in the experiment_plan, under the \"median\" tier assumptions. Let me carefully go through each experiment and predict what results would look like given the median tier parameters.\n\nLet me recall the median tier definition:\n- Real contamination magnitude: c̄ between 0.4–0.9\n- Kendall-τ for G-MFRM: 0.84–0.89\n- Kendall-τ for best baseline: 0.82–0.87\n- Delta τ vs best baseline: 0.01–0.04\n- RMSE reduction vs sequential: 8–25%\n\n\n- Confounding θ-RMSE degradation: 5–20%\n- Scatter Pearson r (sequential bias): 0.25–0.50\n- Convergence max R̂: 1.03–1.08\n- Convergence min ESS: 80–200\n- Wilcoxon p (joint vs seq): 0.001–0.05\n\nNow I'm working through each experiment to predict what the results would show. For exp-001 on multi-judge data collection, I'd expect results focused on data quality and coverage metrics. For exp-002 on ConStat exposure estimation, the results would center on estimation accuracy. I need to continue through the remaining experiments and flesh out what each would demonstrate under these median tier conditions. I'm laying out the experimental roadmap with eleven key studies, each targeting specific aspects of the model's performance and robustness. Now I need to develop concrete predictions for what I expect to find in each experiment at the median performance tier.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11171,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11171},"output_tokens":28,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2d0e975-07c9-4